Here is the commit message:
fixed a bug. mCurPage should be set to null immediately when
 last page is popped, even if there is an transition animation to play

Here is the root cause:
In the page-popping logic, the update of `mCurPage` to `prevPage` (along with the removal of the popped page's view from the container) was deferred until `doFinalWorkForPopPageInternal`, which only executes after the transition animation finishes. This meant that during the animation playback, `mCurPage` still referenced the already-popped page instead of the new current page. Since animations can take time (or in some cases run asynchronously), any code that queried `mCurPage` during that window—such as new page push/pop operations or UI logic depending on the current page state—would receive a stale, incorrect reference to the popped page rather than the actual current page, leading to inconsistent state management and related bugs.

Here is the patch:

   private void popPageInternal(final Page removedPage, boolean animated, boolean hint) {
     final Page prevPage;
     if (mPageStack.size() > 0) {    // this check is always necessary
       prevPage = mPageStack.getLast();

       if (animated && mPageAnimator != null && !removedPage.onPopPageAnimation(removedPage, prevPage, hint)) {
         mPageAnimator.onPopPageAnimation(removedPage, prevPage, hint);
       }

       prevPage.getView().setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
     } else {
       prevPage = null;

       if (animated && mPageAnimator != null && !removedPage.onPopPageAnimation(removedPage, null, hint)) {
         mPageAnimator.onPopPageAnimation(removedPage, null, hint);
       }
     }

+    mContainerView.removeView(removedPage.getView());
+    mCurPage = prevPage;
+
     int animationDuration = removedPage.getAnimationDuration();
     if (animationDuration == -1 && mPageAnimator != null) {
       animationDuration = mPageAnimator.getAnimationDuration();
     }
     if (animated && animationDuration != -1) {
       removedPage.postDelayed(new Runnable() {
         @Override
         public void run() {
           doFinalWorkForPopPageInternal(removedPage, prevPage);
         }
       }, animationDuration);

     } else {
       doFinalWorkForPopPageInternal(removedPage, prevPage);
     }
   }

   private void doFinalWorkForPopPageInternal(Page removedPage, Page prevPage) {
-    mContainerView.removeView(removedPage.getView());
     removedPage.onDetach();
     removedPage.onHidden();
-    mCurPage = prevPage;

     if (prevPage != null) {
       prevPage.onUncovered(removedPage.getReturnData());
     }
   }



